learnings:
  - 'Arky: the three Claude runners have drifted, not just duplicated. Conductor''s ClaudeStreamSession.swift:183 passes --dangerously-skip-permissions with no session id, while flow forbids it. One kernel supervisor is a safety fix, not just tidying.'
  - 'Arky: Paradigm''s events/stream.jsonl ids (ev-<ms>-<rand>, no seq/principal/hash) fail TD-2026-10-14-735''s collision-free requirement; flow''s hash-chained chain table is the best log seed.'
  - 'Arky: Warpline''s agent-shell treats a missing WARPLINE_AGENT_ID as human; flow''s ENV_ALLOW drops it, so (inferred) flow-spawned sessions could pass human-only Warpline checks today.'
  - 'Arky: the kernel must stay tiny (principals/keys, hash-chained log, session supervisor, approval broker, manifest loader, ref resolver); the moat (symbol graph, notebooks, calibration, Warpline engine) lives in userland. Warpline-native sessions = userland boot package + four kernel spawn duties; F4 forbids injecting Warpline teaching beyond one pointer line.'
  - 'Loid (verified): the learning loop is a popularity loop. orchestration.ts:881 increments appliedCount on injection, notebook-loader.ts:148 ranks by it; 384/396 global notebook entries never applied; injection dark since 2026-07-22; calibration empty on a-paradigm; journals fell to 0 since August; 200/200 debates complementary. 8.0 needs honest credited-vs-injected usage, written-back decay, same-symbol contradiction audits, and source-hash staleness.'
